 This leads to Bell's theorem.
Bell proved mathematically that if hidden variables existed, particle connections must obey soem inequalities. 
But to Knowons suprise, experiments violated those inequalities. 
  Hidden variables don't work, not because we can't access them but because they just don't exist until we the measurer, take the measuremennt.
What this  means is that the universe decides at the moment of measurement.
  
